In this improvisational comedy, two very citified New Yorkers are preparing to wed one another on a Vermont farm owned by the girl's aunt. They are all a-dither but must somehow pull everything together with the help of the decidedly calm, slightly bemused, no-nonsense locals. The locals are unimpressed by all the hubbub and are particularly unimpressed by the things the excitable couple want to do to impress their guests from the city in their quest for a memorably different type of wedding. 
